From ed4e2d926eb8a3222aabc12a447fa5a6310a049e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mojavemesa-lgtm <252102886+mojavemesa-lgtm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:33:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] main/postmarketos-base-ui-networkmanager-usb-tethering:
 do not rm -rf the configfs mount point

reactivate_gadget() mounts configfs on /config, cycles the UDC, then runs
"umount /config; rm -rf /config". configfs is a singleton superblock and
the dispatcher script runs many times at once (up, dhcp, reapply events:
about ten runs within seconds after usb0 comes up). The /config mounts
stack, so a umount can leave another instance's mount in place. The
following "rm -rf /config" then walks the live configfs and unlinks the
gadget's function link (configs/c.1/ncm.usb0).

The already bound gadget keeps working, so nothing is noticed until the
UDC is unbound once (for example after a USB host session on a phone
with a dual-role port). The next bind fails with

  Config c/1 of g1 needs at least one function

and USB networking is gone until the next boot.

Use rmdir, which only removes the empty mount point and fails harmlessly
when something is still mounted there.

Seen and tested on a OnePlus 6T (postmarketOS,
postmarketos-base-ui-networkmanager-usb-tethering-51-r0): with the change
the function link survives the parallel runs and the gadget rebinds.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../50-tethering.sh                                           | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/main/postmarketos-base-ui-networkmanager-usb-tethering/50-tethering.sh b/main/postmarketos-base-ui-networkmanager-usb-tethering/50-tethering.sh
index 63f44ff..1bdc1de 100644
--- a/main/postmarketos-base-ui-networkmanager-usb-tethering/50-tethering.sh
+++ b/main/postmarketos-base-ui-networkmanager-usb-tethering/50-tethering.sh
@@ -52,7 +52,9 @@ reactivate_gadget() {
 
 	# Unmount configFS
 	umount /config
-	rm -rf /config
+	# Not rm -rf: if the umount did not remove the last configfs mount, this
+	# would walk the live configfs and delete the gadget's function symlinks.
+	rmdir /config 2>/dev/null || true
 
 	logger -t nm-tethering "configFS unmounted"
 }
